                    {
                        "sense_id": "2269d51e-5285-381c-a196-7d46cb33c313",
                        "entry_id": "c65171e6-60e6-3436-bb67-6dbde8e2dd55",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of something that slips; a slip; a skidding or sudden loosening motion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec15624e-141c-4fe4-8d56-e9517fa410cf",
                                "sense_id": "2269d51e-5285-381c-a196-7d46cb33c313",
                                "text": "slippings and slidings"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3028e05-a0c9-4f22-86f1-b6141bf73e85",
                                "sense_id": "2269d51e-5285-381c-a196-7d46cb33c313",
                                "text": "Experiments on steep inclines in the United States showed that washing the rails with a detergent to remove oil and grease resulted in a marked improvement; but conditioning the rails with a special neutralising chemical completely eliminated slipping on a bank on which it was so common as to necessitate restriction of trainloads."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f57b19bb-bf0e-40f0-8ad6-919684e99244",
                                "sense_id": "2269d51e-5285-381c-a196-7d46cb33c313",
                                "text": "The \"King\" responded well to this treatment and would have maintained 60 m.p.h. up the steepest part had it not been for a brief bout of slipping, which was quickly corrected by Driver Bailes (\"Autumn leaves\", he remarked laconically)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
